/**
 * @defgroup FsceGeo FsceGeo — Forward Sampling Calorimeter Preshower Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR Forward Sampling Calorimeter (FSC)
 *        preshower detector, conceptual tag PRES.
 *
 * @details
 * The Forward Sampling Calorimeter (FSC) preshower is a fine-grained tungsten-based
 * sampling calorimeter located at z ≈ 761.7 cm from the STAR interaction point, co-planar
 * with the Forward Meson Spectrometer (FMS).  Its purpose is to initiate and partially
 * sample electromagnetic showers before they enter the FMS lead-glass calorimeter, thereby
 * improving the electron/photon identification capability at very forward rapidities (η ≳ 2.5).
 *
 * **Geometry overview:**
 * The detector is a rectangular 40 × 80 array of spaghetti-style tower elements (FSCT),
 * each 2.5 × 2.5 cm² in transverse cross-section and 90 cm in depth.  All towers share the
 * WSE (tungsten + polystyrene scintillator + epoxy) mixture at ρ = 8.297 g/cm³, corresponding
 * to a radiation length of approximately 0.87 cm, giving the full tower depth of ~103 X₀.
 * A 6 × 6 central hole is left open for the beam pipe.
 *
 * **Placement:**
 * The container volume FSCE (BOX 50 × 100 × 90 cm) is placed at
 * z = distFromVtx + towerLength = 716.7 + 45.0 = 761.7 cm.
 * Tower positions are generated by a double loop over the 40 × 80 grid; the central
 * 6 × 6 hole is excluded programmatically.  A source comment notes that the BOX container
 * will overlap the beam pipe and should eventually be replaced by a PGON shape.
 *
 * **Sensitive volume:**
 * Each FSCT tower is instrumented with a single hit variable (eloss) covering 0–250 MeV
 * with 16-bit precision.  Particle-tracking thresholds are CUTGAM = 0.5 MeV and
 * CUTELE = 0.15 MeV.
 *
 * There is no @c FsceConfig.xml; the single geometry version (Version = 1) is set in the
 * FSCP @c Fill block.
 *
 * @par Author
 * D. Arkhipkin (arkhipkin\@bnl.gov)
 *
 * @par Created
 * 4 July 2011
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @defgroup FsceGeoV1 FSCEGEO v1 — Production Tower Array
 * @ingroup FsceGeo
 * @brief 40 × 80 array of 2.5 × 2.5 × 90 cm³ tungsten-scintillator towers with a 6 × 6
 *        central beam-pipe aperture, at z ≈ 761.7 cm.
 *
 * @details Activated whenever the @c FSCEGEO module is loaded (single version).
 * The FSCE container (BOX, 50 × 100 × 45 cm half-dimensions) holds 3174 FSCT tower
 * placements.  Each FSCT is a sensitive BOX (1.25 × 1.25 × 45 cm) of WSE material
 * (W 92.3%, C 7.1%, H 0.6%).
 *
 * Key parameters:
 *   - towerWidth  = 1.25 cm (half), towerLength = 45.0 cm (half)
 *   - nTowersX = 20 (half), nTowersY = 40 (half)
 *   - nEmpty = 3 (half-count of central hole in each direction)
 *   - distFromVtx = 716.7 cm
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
